      "1 RMB Coins and Bills",
      "",
      "If you travel in China you will quickly discover something strange.",
      "Why are there some places that have one yuan coins, and other places that have one yuan banknotes?",
      "For example, in Beijing there are only one yuan banknotes, but in Shanghai one yuan banknotes are very rare.",
      "Currently, only Shanghai, Jiangsu, Zhejiang, Shenzhen, and Liaoning use one yuan coins, other places in China all use banknotes.",
      "This difference is related to the weather.",
      "The places that use coins are close to the sea, and it often rains, so the weather is very moist, and banknotes easily break.",
      "In many places that use banknotes it rarely rains, so they don’t need to use coins there."
